From fc9970cb1d56f8e608a8751567ff42dbba582892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Initialise the client RECV_DATA packet pointer

PacketQueue::read() leaves its out-pointer unset when the queue is empty, and
then returns 0, so the copy loop that follows never reads it. GCC 14 cannot
see that and reports -Wmaybe-uninitialized at -Os, which stops a build that
treats warnings as errors (ESP-IDF's default, where gbagate builds this
file). No change in behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014LvpUYFw94JkaNFyrbwJmK
---
 src/sections/rfuProtocol.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sections/rfuProtocol.hpp b/src/sections/rfuProtocol.hpp
index c935711..712daee 100644
--- a/src/sections/rfuProtocol.hpp
+++ b/src/sections/rfuProtocol.hpp
@@ -1965,7 +1965,7 @@ private:
                 else if (state == stClient)
                 {
                     uint32_t cnt = 0;
-                    const uint8_t* p;
+                    const uint8_t* p = nullptr;  // set by read() whenever dlen > 0
                     const uint32_t dlen = m_client.pkt.read(&p);
                     m_buf[cnt++] = dlen;
                     for (uint32_t j = 0; j < (dlen + 3) / 4; j++)
